### LLM Cost Control Tracker API — sample requests
### §14.3 developer workflow: manual probing with curl / .http client
###
### Prerequisites:
### 1. docker compose up -d
### 2. F5 the Tracker.Api project (connects to compose Postgres + telemetry)
### 3. Obtain a valid gateway JWT (see test helper or stub OIDC provider)
###    For local dev with auth disabled, set GatewayAuth:IsEnabled=false in
###    appsettings.Development.json

### ── Budget check (§6.2.1) ──

### Check if a caller is allowed (happy path)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/budget/check
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callerId": "user@example.com",
  "model": "gpt-4o"
}

### Check for an unbudgeted caller (denied)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/budget/check
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callerId": "unbudgeted@example.com"
}

### Check with missing callerId (400 invalid_request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/budget/check
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
}

### Check without auth (401 unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/budget/check
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callerId": "user@example.com"
}

### ── Usage capture (§6.2.2) ──

### Capture a usage event (happy path)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/usage/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callerId": "user@example.com",
  "model": "gpt-4o",
  "tokens": {
    "input": 1000,
    "output": 500,
    "cacheRead": 200,
    "cacheWrite": 0
  },
  "requestId": "req-001"
}

### Capture with unknown model (400 unknown_model)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/usage/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callerId": "user@example.com",
  "model": "nonexistent",
  "tokens": {
    "input": 1000,
    "output": 500,
    "cacheRead": 0,
    "cacheWrite": 0
  }
}

### Capture with idempotent requestId (duplicate — no double accrual)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/usage/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callerId": "user@example.com",
  "model": "gpt-4o",
  "tokens": {
    "input": 1000,
    "output": 500,
    "cacheRead": 0,
    "cacheWrite": 0
  },
  "requestId": "req-001"
}

### ── Pricing file import (§8.3, localhost only) ──

### Import a valid pricing file
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pricing/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "generatedAt": "2026-06-25T12:00:00Z",
  "currency": "USD",
  "unit": "per-1M-tokens",
  "providers": [
    {
      "provider": "openai",
      "models": [
        {
          "model": "gpt-4o",
          "fetchedAt": "2026-06-25T12:00:00Z",
          "prices": {
            "input": 2.50,
            "output": 10.00,
            "cacheRead": 1.25,
            "cacheWrite": null
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### Import an invalid pricing file (negative price — 400 invalid_file)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pricing/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "generatedAt": "2026-06-25T12:00:00Z",
  "currency": "USD",
  "unit": "per-1M-tokens",
  "providers": [
    {
      "provider": "openai",
      "models": [
        {
          "model": "gpt-4o",
          "fetchedAt": "2026-06-25T12:00:00Z",
          "prices": {
            "input": -1.0,
            "output": 10.00,
            "cacheRead": 1.25
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### ── Auth test endpoint (§6.1, M12) ──

### Verify a valid gateway token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── Variables ──

@baseUrl = https://localhost:5001
@token = your-jwt-token-here
